TEXT 480 168 Left 2 ;Set r_x to a low value like 0.005 the voltage maximum is sharper\nand about 13kV peak at the maximum (4.5kV peak for 125A)\nSet r_x to 0.03 gives a flat maximum of voltage\nand about 2.2kv peak
TEXT -8 176 Left 2 ;For steady state simulation of a petersen \nsee also peterson_unsymm.asc in the\nloadflow examples folder
TEXT 568 128 Left 2 ;Change between 120A and 125A
TEXT 248 184 Left 2 ;Due to voltage drop at inner transformer impedance\nthe voltage of the starpoint is below\nthe nominal phase voltage at fault occurrence\ntherefore the petersen automatic\nhas to set the pet current to a higher value\nwhich is done automatically by resonance tuning\nfor maximal starpoint voltage
TEXT 248 272 Left 2 ;Uphase,nominal=89.8kV peak (110kV Pet/125A)\nUphase at starpoint after fault=87.5kV ->\nIpet has to be set to a higher value\nfrom the automatic to compensate this
